## JRE — Sirf Chalana Hai Toh Ye Kaafi Hai

**JRE = JVM + Libraries**

```
JRE =
├── JVM (ByteCode run karne ke liye)
└── Java Libraries & APIs
    (ready-made code jo Java programs use karte hain)
    jaise — System.out.println() bhi ek library call hai!
```

**Kab use karo?**
- Jab sirf Java program **chalana** ho — develop nahi karna
- Normal user ke computer par JRE hota hai
- Developer ke computer par JDK hota hai (JRE automatically aata hai)

---

## JDK — Developer Ka Poora Toolkit

**JDK = JRE + Development Tools**

```
JDK =
├── JRE (JVM + Libraries)
└── Development Tools:
    ├── javac     ← compiler (.java → .class)
    ├── java      ← launcher (program run karta hai)
    ├── javadoc   ← documentation generate karta hai
    ├── jdb       ← debugger
    └── jar       ← files package karta hai
```

**Kab use karo?**
- Jab Java mein **code likhna + compile karna + run karna** ho
- Har developer ke machine par JDK hona chahiye

